    'eyes-brann-whole-1121': { pri: 2, group: G2, title: 'BRANN SILVERSANDS WHOLE: his drawn fight figure with the JUMPING CHOP, beside his new town figure, the axe on his shoulder (11-21)', pt: 'the story build lane, 2026-11-21 (the cutter, cutter-1121; tools/road-town-sheet.py brann_p1; tools/silversands-fight-sheet.py brann_p2; deep16/js/save.js SV.LOOK brann)',
      obj: 'In the gallery, step Brann\'s fight rows beside his town figure: does the jumping chop leave the floor and land on frame 4?',
      url: 'deep16/?gallery&shelf=creatures&rows=brann_p2,brann_p1&beside&lvl=3&fresh=1121bw',
      look: 'NEW, the art desk\'s ART-145 town figure (art-wanted 88\'s last block), on your "fresh isn\'t empty, more incoming as well", beside his ART-145-COMBAT fight figure of 11-20 (never shown till now). THE TOWN FIGURE: young Brann in splint and his steel cap, no shield, the bearded battleaxe resting on its butt at his right side at idle and riding his right shoulder as he walks; cut at a dwarf\'s 38 px in all eight facings (SW, W, NW the mirrors, the axe to the other shoulder there). The art desk flags its E and rear NE walks for gait review: cut as drawn. THE FIGHT FIGURE: the battleaxe in both hands, rows idle, walk, ATTACK -- the jumping chop: the guard, the coil, both feet off the floor at the top, the chop coming down still in the air, landed deep with the blade to the floor on frame 4, the step back -- flinch, fall (the axe dropped beside him), prone; each frame on the art desk\'s own ground line, so the jump leaves the floor. He fights in it wherever he is a guest (the Pocket DM, ?vs=brann:5); his town figure stands nowhere yet (the muster yard is not on the grid). Judge: is this Brann, both ways, and is it a jump and a real chop?' },
