    'eyes-generic-costumes-1028': { pri: 2, group: G2, title: 'The unnamed in costume: the generic man and woman from the art desk\'s ART-122, each in their job\'s look on the counter\'s screen (10-28)', pt: 'the bestiary, the fourth cutter seat (tools/portrait-sheet.py pt_genman, pt_genwoman; js/counter.js C.GENERIC) · eyes',
      obj: 'Talk with Silverton\'s gate hand, Hex gamblers and guano scrapers — is each the same face in their job\'s costume?',
      url: 'deep16/?portraits&who=towns1,towns2,hexpatron1,hexpatron2,gambler1,gambler2,bartenderS,bartenderE,towns3,ropewar,towns5,crew2,scraper1,scraper2,scrapeboss,drivecrew,guard1,dunmoreLine,towns6,towns7,seepcrew2,seepcrew1&fresh=1028m',
      look: 'Your "as a specific person with each function as a costume/look they have": the art desk\'s generic man and woman (the townsfolk\'s faces), one page each of the unnamed people who used to speak on a plain card -- now on the counter\'s screen in the costume of their job, saying what they always said: the townsman and townswoman in their own clothes, the Hex\'s drinkers, gamblers and barkeeps, the hired hands, the shaft hands, the guano scrapers and their boss, the drive spear, the gate hand and Dunmore\'s line in a guard\'s cap, the clerk, the factor\'s man, the Glowseep\'s light crews. OK through the 22 looks. The man is the same face on every page, the woman too (their likeness to the townsfolk figures is the art desk\'s open question). A wide prop runs off the portrait\'s panel (the scraper\'s lamp). The crawler hand\'s costume waits for someone to wear it.' },
    'eyes-falstaff-face-1029': { pri: 2, group: G2, title: 'Falstaff\'s talking portrait from the art desk\'s ART-123: his idle, the four moods and his ledger (10-29)', pt: 'the bestiary, the cutter seat of 10-29 (tools/portrait-sheet.py pt_falstaff; js/counter.js C.VENDORS) · eyes',
      obj: 'Knock at the factor house\'s west door and offer Falstaff a spell sheet — can you tell his four moods apart?',
      url: 'deep16/?portraits&who=falstaff&fresh=1029a',
      look: 'Your "pinged the art dept for his north facings": Falstaff, the factor\'s clerk of the factor house (pin 7a), the last door keeper who spoke on a plain card -- now on his own face, the art desk\'s ART-123: a watchful man of middle years in a long dark coat and brown waistcoat, an off-white scarf high over his burned throat. Step his idle (a breath and a blink), the four moods (attentive, welcoming, skeptical, concerned: the art desk\'s own notes call them subdued -- say if they read alike) and his work (he opens a ledger, writes a line, closes it). In town: E at his door, the factor house\'s west door, and he says his first-game word on this face. His stills drew a bevelled counter top; it is cut off as Aldwin\'s was.' },
